WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.901
Dressed as a beggar, Robin walked along the road for most of the afternoon.

2
00:00:07.902 --> 00:00:11.324
"I should head back to Sherwood Forest soon," he said.

3
00:00:11.325 --> 00:00:15.009
"But I'd like to have one more adventure."

4
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:19.977
So he looked up and down the road, hoping to see someone approaching.

5
00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:24.008
Soon a thin man came riding along on a skinny horse.

6
00:00:24.009 --> 00:00:28.972
The man was wearing strange-looking clogs with very thick soles.

7
00:00:28.973 --> 00:00:33.526
Robin stared at the man. "I know him!" he thought.

8
00:00:33.527 --> 00:00:38.730
"That's the wicked corn merchant who cheated the poor!"

9
00:00:38.731 --> 00:00:42.787
The corn merchant had bought a huge supply of corn.

10
00:00:42.788 --> 00:00:46.712
Then he held onto it to create a corn shortage.

11
00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:52.215
When everyone in the village was desperate for corn, he sold it at a high price.

12
00:00:52.216 --> 00:00:56.248
And he'd done this greedy thing several times.

13
00:00:56.249 --> 00:01:00.320
When the merchant approached, Robin stepped into the road.

14
00:01:00.321 --> 00:01:04.897
"Stop!" cried Robin, grabbing the horse's reins.

15
00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:07.847
"Who are you?" demanded the merchant.

16
00:01:07.848 --> 00:01:13.501
"Just a poor beggar," said Robin. "Have pity and give me a few pennies for bread."

17
00:01:13.502 --> 00:01:17.075
"Get away from me!" yelled the corn merchant.

18
00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:20.690
"Beggars like you belong in prison."

19
00:01:20.691 --> 00:01:24.766
"We both take money from other people," said Robin.

20
00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.072
"Neither one of us does honest work.

21
00:01:27.073 --> 00:01:31.258
We're like brothers, except you're rich and I'm poor."

22
00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:36.091
"Don't talk to me like that!" said the corn merchant angrily.

23
00:01:36.092 --> 00:01:39.818
"As for giving you money, I don't have any.

24
00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:43.592
I don't dare travel near Sherwood Forest with money.

25
00:01:43.593 --> 00:01:47.772
That thief Robin Hood hasn't been captured yet!"

26
00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:51.180
Robin showed no reaction to his name.

27
00:01:51.181 --> 00:01:54.654
Instead he motioned for the merchant to bend down.

28
00:01:54.655 --> 00:01:56.873
"Look at me," he whispered.

29
00:01:56.874 --> 00:02:00.249
"There's not one bit of dirt on my face or hands.

30
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:04.585
Do you really think I'm a beggar? I'm as honest as you are."

31
00:02:04.586 --> 00:02:09.510
Robin opened his shirt to reveal a small bag hanging around his neck.

32
00:02:09.511 --> 00:02:12.507
"I'm hiding this from Robin Hood."

33
00:02:12.508 --> 00:02:17.230
The merchant's eyes widened as Robin showed him some gold coins.

34
00:02:17.231 --> 00:02:20.827
"Put that money away, you fool!" said the merchant.

35
00:02:20.828 --> 00:02:24.919
"If Robin Hood catches you, he'll take everything you have.

36
00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.987
He hates dishonest beggars as much as greedy merchants."

37
00:02:29.988 --> 00:02:35.518
"Oh, I had no idea!" Robin pretended to be surprised.

38
00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:40.060
"May I walk with you? We seem to be going in the same direction."

39
00:02:40.061 --> 00:02:43.656
"Well, all right," said the corn merchant.

40
00:02:43.657 --> 00:02:53.140
"I don't mind your company, now that I know you're an honest man."

41
00:02:53.141 --> 00:02:58.641
The two men traveled in silence until they reached the outskirts of Sherwood Forest.

42
00:02:58.642 --> 00:03:00.824
Then the merchant turned to Robin.

43
00:03:00.825 --> 00:03:03.911
"We're getting close to where Robin Hood lives.

44
00:03:03.912 --> 00:03:07.746
Here's where you're in the greatest danger, my friend."

45
00:03:07.747 --> 00:03:12.413
"I wish I had as little money with me as you do," said Robin.

46
00:03:12.414 --> 00:03:15.813
"I'm afraid Robin Hood will steal my gold."

47
00:03:15.814 --> 00:03:18.967
The merchant laughed and winked at Robin.

48
00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:24.182
"I'll tell you a secret. I have more money with me than you do.

49
00:03:24.183 --> 00:03:29.351
But it's hidden in a place Robin Hood will never find."

50
00:03:29.352 --> 00:03:33.220
Robin opened his eyes wide. "Really?"

51
00:03:33.221 --> 00:03:36.955
The merchant nodded. "See my shoes?

52
00:03:36.956 --> 00:03:40.449
The soles of my clogs are actually boxes.

53
00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.149
I've hidden ninety pounds in gold coins in each one."

54
00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:52.117
"In the soles of your clogs?" Robin laughed until he cried.

55
00:03:52.118 --> 00:03:55.432
The merchant stared at Robin with a frown.

56
00:03:55.433 --> 00:03:57.712
"There's nothing to laugh at!"

57
00:03:57.713 --> 00:04:00.345
But Robin was still chuckling.

58
00:04:00.346 --> 00:04:02.623
"I really like those clogs.

59
00:04:02.624 --> 00:04:04.612
Take them off and give them to me.

60
00:04:04.613 --> 00:04:07.947
If you don't take them off, I'll summon my friends."

61
00:04:07.948 --> 00:04:12.372
The merchant turned pale. "Who are you really?"

62
00:04:12.373 --> 00:04:15.617
"Everyone calls me Robin Hood!"

63
00:04:15.618 --> 00:04:19.516
The merchant shook with fear as he removed his clogs.

64
00:04:19.517 --> 00:04:23.361
Robin made him open the soles and count out the coins.

65
00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:27.345
"Now get out of here!" Robin said sternly.

66
00:04:27.346 --> 00:04:30.893
"I've heard many stories about how you've cheated the poor.

67
00:04:30.894 --> 00:04:35.549
If I hear any more of these stories, you'll be in real trouble!"

68
00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.799
The merchant rode away as fast as he could.

69
00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.381
That night in Sherwood Forest the fire stayed lit for a long time.

70
00:04:44.382 --> 00:04:52.258
Around the glowing fire, Robin and Little John entertained the men with stories of their adventures as a beggar and a friar.

71
00:04:52.259 --> 00:04:55.830
The men listened closely, laughing at their tales.

72
00:04:55.831 --> 00:04:59.033
When they were finished, Friar Tuck spoke up.

73
00:04:59.034 --> 00:05:06.024
"I still believe that the life of the friar is happier than the life of the beggar."

74
00:05:06.025 --> 00:05:10.357
Will Scarlet shook his head. "I think Robin's day was more fun.

75
00:05:10.358 --> 00:05:13.789
He tricked those beggars and that nasty corn merchant."

76
00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:18.878
The other men quickly put in their opinions, arguing loudly.

77
00:05:18.879 --> 00:05:22.667
Some agreed with Friar Tuck, and others agreed with Will.

78
00:05:22.668 --> 00:05:25.736
But Robin and Little John just laughed.

79
00:05:25.737 --> 00:05:30.713
They'd both had entertaining adventures!

